    skos:definition "decomposed felspar of the granite, a fine potter's clay largely used in ceramic manufactures, being first artificially cleaned and prepared in Cornwall. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 99]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "doc_china_clay" ;
    skos:prefLabel "China Clay"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0506 (Chemical Manufactures and Products Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 99."@en ;
    <ontology/attestationBasis/#resource> "document_attested" ;
